{#
  Coverage band — a full-bleed grayscale map with the counties we serve shaded
  on top, and the claim itself set over the middle of it.

  Unlike coverage-map.njk (the impressionistic heat-map on /case-studies/) this
  one is real cartography: an actual Google basemap.

  Two ways it can draw, picked here rather than in JS:

  1. With GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY set — the Maps JavaScript API, desaturated
     through the Maps style array, with the county polygons from
     /assets/coverage-counties.json shaded on top. The style array does the
     greying rather than a CSS filter, because a filter would grey the county
     shading out too, and the shading is the whole point.

  2. Without a key — the keyless Google Maps embed, exactly as /contact/ uses,
     framed on the South East and greyed with a CSS filter. No counties are
     shaded (the embed cannot draw polygons), so this is the weaker of the two:
     a real map of the right patch of England behind the claim, standing in
     until the key lands.

  Either way the band is deliberately non-interactive: it is a statement, not a
  tool. /contact/ is where a map you can actually drive lives.
#}
<section class="coverage-band{% if not maps.apiKey %} coverage-band--embed{% endif %}" aria-labelledby="coverage-band-title">

  {# The map paints itself in here. aria-hidden because the heading beside it
     already states the coverage in words; a screen reader gains nothing from
     an unlabelled tile canvas. #}
  <div class="coverage-band__map"
       {% if maps.apiKey %}data-coverage-map
       data-maps-key="{{ maps.apiKey }}"
       data-counties-src="/assets/coverage-counties.json"{% endif %}
       aria-hidden="true">
    {% if not maps.apiKey %}
      {# ll + z rather than q: a query would drop a pin, and a pin in the
         middle of the band would sit right behind the heading. tabindex="-1"
         keeps the frame out of the tab order, since there is nothing in it to
         operate. #}
      <iframe class="coverage-band__frame"
              src="https://maps.google.com/maps?ll=51.15,-0.15&amp;z=9&amp;output=embed"
              title="Map of the South East of England"
              loading="lazy"
              tabindex="-1"
              referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"></iframe>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  <div class="coverage-band__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="container coverage-band__overlay">
    <h2 id="coverage-band-title" class="coverage-band__title">
      {# `x | safe or "default"` does NOT fall through — the filter runs first and
         yields an empty SafeString. Default inside the parens, filter outside. #}
      {{ (coverageBandTitle or "Covering Surrey, Sussex, Kent <span class='em'>and the South East.</span>") | safe }}
    </h2>
    {# The page's way out, under the claim, when the page asks for it
       (`coverageActions`). The home page does (14/10/26): this band and an
       enquiry section after it said "where we work, then how to start" twice
       in a row, so the enquiry's buttons moved up here and it went. #}
    {% if coverageActions %}
    <div class="coverage-band__actions">
      <a class="btn-inquiry btn-inquiry--lg" href="/enquiry/">Book a site survey <span class="btn-inquiry__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a>
      <a class="btn-line btn-line--lg" href="tel:{{ site.tel }}">Call {{ site.phone }} <span class="btn-line__arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></span></a>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

</section>
